-# Task 3 report: barcode capture and item details
-
-## Implemented
-
-- Added an optional barcode field to item create, edit, and detail views, including copied display and validation at 80 characters.
-- Routed the camera scanner result into the regular item form. Added scanning/detected/error feedback and retained manual entry when camera access or catalog lookup is unavailable.
-- Added optional numeric barcode catalog lookup, explicit candidate selection, and duplicate-item navigation. Candidate fields only prefill empty values; internal alphanumeric codes and leading zeroes remain supported.
-- Persisted manufacturer and model number on standard item creation. Extended template-based item creation to persist barcode while keeping omitted fields optional and preserving template defaults.
-- Added frontend helper/API tests and focused repository tests.
-
-## Verification
-
-- `git diff --check`: passed.
-- `frontend/locales/en.json` JSON parse using PowerShell `ConvertFrom-Json`: passed.
-- Go tests: not run successfully. The previous focused invocation stopped before tests because the required Go modules were absent locally and `proxy.golang.org` DNS/network access was unavailable. The cached Go executable path was also not present in this checkout.
-- Frontend Vitest, `pnpm typecheck`, and `pnpm lint:ci`: blocked before project scripts load. pnpm cannot resolve the nested frontend workspace path (`EPERM: operation not permitted, realpath ...\frontend`) and attempts to install dependencies; no local node_modules/test binaries are present. No network retry or permission escalation was used.
-
-The test assertions were added before implementation, but RED/GREEN execution could not be observed because of the tooling limitations above.
-
